# Pilot Batch 001 is identified by SHA-256, in its handoff manifest and in
# `question-bank/pilot-compatibility.e2e.test.ts`. A line-ending conversion
# would change those bytes and fail the integrity check for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the content, so these files are never converted.
nexus-pilot-batch-001.candidates.json -text
nexus-pilot-batch-001.candidates.r2.json -text

# Knowledgebase corpus records, registries, schema and source registry are
# identified by SHA-256 in `knowledge-corpus/manifests/corpus-manifest.json`, and
# `kb-manifest.mjs --check` compares those hashes. A line-ending conversion on a
# checkout would change the bytes and report corpus drift for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the content, so these files are never converted.
knowledge-corpus/**/*.json -text
